{"thought": "Spec is clear. I'll implement using a regex to split on separators, then split camel boundaries (lowercase/digit followed by uppercase). Digits stay attached to preceding letters. Let me write the implementation.", "action": {"tool": "edit_file", "args": {"path": "src/textkit/split_identifier.py", "old": "    raise NotImplementedError", "new": "    import re

    # Replace separators with a space so we can split on them uniformly.
    normalized = re.sub(r"[\s_\-\.]+", " ", name)
    words: List[str] = []
    for chunk in normalized.split():
        # Split a camel/Pascal chunk into words: a new word starts where a
        # lowercase letter or digit is followed by an uppercase letter.
        parts = re.findall(r"[A-Z]+(?![a-z])|[A-Z][a-z]*|\d+|[a-z]+", chunk)
        for part in parts:
            word = part.lower()
            if word:
                words.append(word)
    return words"}}, "messages": []}

